Although entirely unrelated to NetHack, this reminds me of a scene in my
early days of ADOM.

One of the first quests was to find the puppy dog of a young girl, which
got lost in the wilderness. You had to dive into a dungeon and rescue the
dog within a certain time span; if you were late, you found only the
corpse. 

I thought it would be a neat idea to present the dead dog to the girl, so
that she can bury it or mourn it or whatever, but it turned out that the
author had forgotten to implement code for this special case and the game
fell back to the general routine of "Hero gives edible item to peaceful
NPC":

"The tiny girl eagerly grabs the uncursed cute dog corspe! The tiny
girl devours the uncursed cute dog corpse."

I never looked at her quite the same way.

